=what is mongodb query api
it is a interface you use to interact with data stored in mongodb
its 3 main areas of functionality
-crud operations
-the aggregation frameword
-specialized query features

=the mongodb query api used to perform
Adhoc queries with mongosh, Compass, VS Code, or a MongoDB driver for the programming language you use.
Data transformations using aggregation pipelines.
Document join support to combine data from different collections.
Graph and geospatial queries.
Full-text search.
Indexing to improve MongoDB query performance.
Time series analysis.


=BASICS OF COMPASS
A>the main home interface of compass have some options like connections, my queries, tabs etc
by default in localhost there are three databases 
first is admin which is for security, user roles and admin commands, essential for security.
second is config stores metadata for distributed clusters, essential for cluster health
third is local for server specific logs and startup data, essential for replication

B>so databases in mongodb may consist of many collection which may consists of many documents which may consists of many fields.
when you click in any database there comes a insert document option and there you can add new fields with json syntax
also you can use mongodb shell to run commands this feature is given by compass
and another way to run mongodb commands is window terminal but for this first type mongosh which means mongodb shell to be connect with server








****************************************USING MONGODB CAMPASS AND MONDODB SHELL FOR FOLLOWING
1.
Mongodb compass interface
Create new database in seleted connection by + sign
And there is _id automatically assigned to each document for unique identification and can be set manually 
Add data option to insert new document
Always follow the correct json format to write data
There is features to open multiple tab in compass
Open mongodb shell option on top right for shell
In MongoDB, a database is not actually created until it gets content!
In MongoDB, a collection is not actually created until it gets content!

2.
Basic Shell commands (show, use, find)
show dbs =this shows all the databases present in the server
use db_name =this is used to switched to the desired database
db =this show the name of database which is currently active to perform operation with
show collections =this shows collection presents inside the database

FIND()*********************************************
db.collection_name.find() =here db refers to the current database you are connected wtih
                                collection_name is specific collection you want to query
                                .find() retrieves documents from that collection
by default, find() returns all documents in the collection
you can pass a query object inside find() to filter results, THIS is querying data from database
db.users.find({"name": "nikesh"})
output =[ { _id: ObjectId('69a9e3bfdcbf51f18e9194c8'), name: 'nikesh' } ]
db.collection_name.findOne() =to select only one document This method accepts a query object. If left empty, it will return the first document it finds.


3.
commands for collections
show collections =list all collections in the current db
db.createCollection("collection_name") =create a collection
db.oldcollection_name.renameCollection("newcollection_name") =rename collection name
db.collection_name.drop() =delete given collection

4.
window terminal 
mongosh =means mongodb shell to connect with server and it is the first command to type in terminal of window to use mongodb
if you trying first time then by default maybe you see test db

will if you switched to any db that is not present but in command prompt it shows that it is switched
to that db then it will created in the server when you put any collection inside it
like
use new_db
new_db.createCollection("users")
here new_db is databases, users is collection, and each row inside it is a document stored in json format
and each key value pair is field-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------








************CRUD commands
1. CREATE
db.collection_name.insertOne({ __ : " "})
insert a single document and this method inserts a single object into the database
insert value inside the document collection even if the collection is not present previously and if present then also not issue at all

db.collection_name.insertMany([{ __ : " "}, {}, {},.....])
insert multiple documents at once and this method inserts an array of objects into the databases
when typing in the shell, after opening an object with curly braces "{" you can press enter to start a new line
in the editor without executing the command. the command will execute when you press enter after closing the braces


2.READ
db.collection_name.find() =retrive all documents in the collection, return a cursor object
db.collection_name.find().pretty() =same ad find() but formats the output in more readable way
db.collection_name.findOne({__:" "}) =retrieve the first document that matches the filter condition and if now specification is given then it output the first field of the document
PROJECTION**********
projection is the way to control which fields are returned when you run a find() or findOne() query. 
By default mongoDB returns the entire document but with projection you can include or exclude specific fields.

3.UPDATE
db.collectionName.updateOne({ __ : " "},{$set:{ __ : " "}}) =updates a single document that matches the filter. $set modifies only specified fields
inside first{} is for filter
db.users.updatetMany({__:” “},{$set:{__:” “}}) =updates multiple documents that match the filter
like 
input: db.emp.updateOne({name:'a'},{$set:{name:'hazif'}})
ouput:
{
  acknowledged: true,
  insertedId: null,
  matchedCount: 1,
  modifiedCount: 1,
  upsertedCount: 0
}
Inside second{} is for updated value

4.DELETE
=db.collectionName.deleteone({__:” “}) =delete a single document that matches the filter
=db.collectionName.deleteMany({__:” “}) =delete all documents that match the filter

EXAMPLES*****************************
// CREATE
db.users.insertOne({ name: "Alice", age: 25 });
db.users.insertMany([{ name: "Bob" }, { name: "Charlie" }]);

// READ
db.users.find();
db.users.find().pretty();
db.users.findOne({ name: "Alice" });

// UPDATE
db.users.updateOne({ name: "Alice" }, { $set: { age: 26 } });
db.users.updateMany({ age: { $lt: 30 } }, { $set: { status: "young" } });

// DELETE
db.users.deleteOne({ name: "Bob" });
db.users.deleteMany({ status: "young" });














